  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "Six trees are equally spaced along one side of a straight road. The distance from the first tree to the fourth is \\(60\\) feet. What is the distance in feet between the first and last trees?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(90\\)",
    "B": "\\(100\\)",
    "C": "\\(105\\)",
    "D": "\\(120\\)",
    "E": "\\(140\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Equal spacing suggests counting the gaps between trees. From the first tree to the fourth there are \\(3\\) gaps, so each gap measures\n\\[\n60\\div3=20\\text{ feet}.\n\\]\nFrom the first tree to the sixth and last tree there are \\(5\\) gaps. Thus the distance is\n\\[\n5\\times20=100\\text{ feet},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
